  {
   "s": "NYKAA",
   "n": "FSN E-Commerce Ventures Limited",
   "cat": "General Updates",
   "when": "2026-09-24 17:03",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "**1. Most Important Fact**  \nFSN E-Commerce Ventures Limited (Nykaa) has completed the acquisition of a 51% shareholding (on a fully diluted basis) in Aminu Wellness Private Limited (\"Aminu\"), and with the shares credited to Nykaa's demat account, Aminu has officially become a subsidiary of the company.\n\n**2. Key Numbers**  \n* **Stake Acquired:** 51% shareholding on a fully diluted basis.  \n* *Note:* No financial metrics (deal consideration, transaction value, revenue, or margins) are stated in this document.\n\n**3. Management Guidance / Forward-Looking Statements**  \n* None stated in the filing.\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**  \n* No immediate shareholder action required.  \n* Watch for the financial consolidation of Aminu Wellness in subsequent quarterly results and commentary on business synergies within Nykaa's personal care/wellness segment.\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**  \n* **Neutral to mildly positive:** Formally closes a previously announced acquisition, securing majority control of a wellness brand without revealing any unexpected deal terms."
  },
  {
   "s": "COALINDIA",
   "n": "Coal India Limited",
   "cat": "Disclosure under SEBI Takeover Regulations",
   "when": "2026-09-24 12:12",
   "sent": "neutral",
   "txt": "**1. Single Most Important Fact**\nCoal India Limited submitted an annual declaration under Regulation 31(4) of SEBI (SAST) Regulations, 2011, confirming that promoters (referencing Central Mine Planning & Design Institute Limited) along with Persons Acting in Concert (PAC) have not made any direct or indirect encumbrances during the financial year, other than those already disclosed.\n\n**2. Key Numbers**\n* No financial numbers, order values, or percentage deltas are stated in this document.\n\n**3. Management Guidance & Forward-Looking Statements**\n* None present.\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* No action required; this is a routine annual statutory non-encumbrance confirmation.\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n* **Neutral**: Standard procedural regulatory compliance filing confirming no undisclosed share pledges/encumbrances."
  },
  {
   "s": "BDL",
   "n": "Bharat Dynamics Limited",
   "cat": "Bagging/Receiving of orders/contracts",
   "when": "2026-09-23 18:11",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "**1. Most Important Fact**\nBharat Dynamics Limited (BDL) has signed a contract worth **Rs 810.79 crore** with the Ministry of Defence for the supply of Satellite Smart Anti Airfield Weapons (SAT-SAAW) and associated equipment for the Indian Air Force (IAF) under the Buy (Indian-IDDM) category.\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**\n* **Total Contract Value / Consideration:** Rs 810.79 crore\n* **Indigenous Content:** 60%\n* **Execution Period:** Between 2027\u201328 and 2028\u201329\n*(Note: As this is an order receipt disclosure, no P&L figures such as revenue, EBITDA, or PAT were provided).*\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance / Forward Statements**\n* Delivery of the SAT-SAAW systems is scheduled between **2027\u20132028 and 2028\u20132029**.\n* The weapon is designed and developed by DRDO to be launched from platforms like Jaguar, Hawk, and Su-30 MKI to neutralise enemy airfields from stand-off ranges.\n* Sub-systems targeted for indigenisation include the Initial Measurement Unit, Long Impact Delay Fuse, and Twin Store Carrier under the *Aatmanirbharta* initiative.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* **Delayed Revenue Recognition:** Execution is back-ended (commencing only in FY28 through FY29), meaning it will not contribute to near-term earnings.\n* **Execution & Production Readiness:** Monitor development, testing, and production ramp-up milestones leading into the FY28\u2013FY29 delivery window.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n**Positive** \u2014 Expands the defence order book with a high-indigenous-content, precision-guided munition contract, providing solid long-term revenue visibility despite the deferred execution timeline."
  },
  {
   "s": "MAZDOCK",
   "n": "Mazagon Dock Shipbuilders Limited",
   "cat": "Change in Director(s)",
   "when": "2026-09-23 11:57",
